{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Scope\n- Refit the Spatial Studio right Inspector around selected-object identity, quick actions, common edits, spatial relationships and scene settings. All three right-rail destinations are functional and keyboard operable.\n- Display Guided, Standard and Engineering as distinct depths while retaining the persisted `GUIDED` / `DETAILED` / `ENGINEERING` contract. Preserve canonical edit/history, autosave, locks and viewport tools.\n- Inventory every existing right-side capability in the property-preservation matrix and update affected guide, product/status documentation and changelog.\n- Identify removed selections and unapplied Assistant objects explicitly; retain Undo restoration and routes to existing objects or scene settings.\n- Preview Inspector rotation and scale on the canvas while the slider moves, then record one canonical transform history edit on release.\n\n## Source-bound local evidence\n- Product source candidate `e007eb8c3e71a6dc6a7c63c953f0b39a81de501a` was built in a task-owned isolated checkout. Two dedicated Chromium journeys pass, including deletion/Undo, normal-motion mobile keyboard navigation, accessibility inspection, and a live scale drag before history commit; task-owned browser/server cleanup passes. The [before](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/codex/parallax-sc-00b-inspector/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00b/candidate-e007eb8c/scale-before-drag.png) and [during](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/codex/parallax-sc-00b-inspector/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/evidence/sc-00b/candidate-e007eb8c/scale-live-preview-before-commit.png) images show the canvas change while Undo is disabled; release creates one Undo step.\n- Product Experience replay against protected base `99a2babaefbbe051de0352c4aca22c8723b743b8` passes 12 desktop/mobile normal/reduced contexts across three affected contracts, with 96 actual-application captures and cleanup PASS. Its source digest is `14abbe352d55b68943e4d96b7b14853d64da3e0c843a41ca6f41aa8d61fc39a8` and contract digest is `021f84450837f1b2e0698c71a9bfcb5142d1f551cd00e58678b87422f4345b57`; the current evidence commit `d9e04166fb0df26a6985187152cd151848b6b270` has the same digests.\n- Thirteen focused component tests pass, including nonzero transform-axis and yaw preservation, invalid selection Undo, unapplied-preview identification, and multiple scale preview samples followed by one history edit. TypeScript, targeted lint, Product Experience contract tests, documentation validation and Feature Catalog sync/validation pass. An earlier affected-browser suite passed five tests with four fixture-gated skips.\n- Owner-review captures and failed/intermediate receipts are in [the candidate review](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/codex/parallax-sc-00b-inspector/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/SC00B_Inspector_Candidate_Review.md); [the property matrix](https://github.com/Kgray44/treasurehuntSoT/blob/codex/parallax-sc-00b-inspector/Development_Docs/Projects/Project_Parallax/SC00B_Property_Capability_Matrix.md) records preserved controls and edit paths.\n\n## Open gates\nThis remains a draft candidate. The review record lists each requested selection type and its current-source evidence or remaining gate. SC-00's typed room-feature/group selection, SC-01's versioned Environment/Scene Manager, SC-02's element types, and SC-00C's Library surface require additive Inspector integration and combined actual-browser checks. The Product Experience workflow's independent visual review, ordinary Sounding Line, protected integration, landed smoke and owner visual decision are not claimed.\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:38:45Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:38:45Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Refit Parallax Spatial Inspector around contextual authoring","oid":"827bf807f06852a4343f2352581b1c407c44552b"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:39:16Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:39:16Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Complete Inspector experience return outcome","oid":"d596f6a5684dc1f5c7efd762c8ecf832200c8de1"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:39:35Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:39:35Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Scope Inspector outcome to its own journey","oid":"2ba73933f07dd112dbde7d0a62ec17cd751e464d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:40:06Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:40:06Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Use meaningful Inspector outcome predicate","oid":"847f54db64309964be25d040779e600349f9bc84"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:50:02Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:50:02Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Verify mobile Inspector destination visibly opens","oid":"79d135c7a9bb83b87c50991da3cd3e550da6fc15"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:52:44Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:52:44Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Give responsive Inspector overlay a usable grid span","oid":"7130920598a8b63e97a948cf3eab001dcdf360dc"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-15T04:56:50Z","authors":[{"email":"kkidsgray@icloud.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzczMDEx","login":"Kgray44","name":"Kgray44"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-15T04:56:50Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Clarify Engineering controls and compact precision inputs","oid":"ca48a6c767fe36240610c02fb857c9d81f71c385"},{"author